# Pin the interpreter to 3.13.
#
# pyproject.toml declares requires-python = ">=3.13" with no upper bound, so
# without this file uv resolves to the newest CPython it can find. When 3.15.0
# was released it did exactly that, and the versions pinned in uv.lock
# (lxml 6.0.2, numpy 2.4.1, pandas 3.0.0, pikepdf 10.2.0) publish no cp315
# wheels. uv fell back to building them from source and the transform pipeline
# failed on the missing libxml2/libxslt build dependencies.
#
# Revisit once those packages ship wheels for a newer interpreter and the lock
# has been regenerated against them.
3.13
